sequenceDiagram
    title autofde_lab_planner (generalized SOTA target) — one diagnosis+mitigation trial

    participant H as SREGym Harness
    participant F as Cluster State Fetcher
    participant S as Structural Anomaly Scanner
    participant SIG as Symptom Signature Builder
    participant CL as Case Library (CBR)
    participant R as DSPy Reasoning Fallback
    participant G as Groq API
    participant M as Remediation Dispatcher
    participant K as Kubernetes Cluster
    participant O as OCEL Telemetry

    H->>F: trial start (namespace, app)
    F->>K: kubectl get -o json (every kind present, not a fixed list)
    K-->>F: real cluster state
    F->>O: record fetch event
    F->>S: raw state
    S->>S: diff vs baseline, per kind, one uniform algorithm
    S->>SIG: typed anomalies (or none)

    alt no anomaly found
        SIG->>H: diagnosis = "no anomaly detected" (honest, not forced)
    else anomaly found
        SIG->>CL: symptom signature
        CL->>CL: Jaccard match vs stored AbstractCases

        alt case library hit (>= threshold)
            CL->>M: rebind template to THIS trial's real object names
            Note over CL,M: same template, different real target — genuine generalization, not replay
        else case library miss
            SIG->>R: symptom signature + real fault taxonomy + structured checklist
            R->>G: real LLM call, grounded (never open-ended)
            G-->>R: classified diagnosis + proposed commands
            R->>O: record real diagnosis event
            R->>M: diagnosis + commands
        end

        M->>K: kubectl patch/rollout/scale (real remediation)
        K-->>M: real outcome
        M->>O: record real mitigation event
        M->>H: submit diagnosis + mitigation

        alt outcome CONFIRMED success
            M->>CL: abstract_raw_case() -- generalize, strip concrete names, store as new AbstractCase
            Note over M,CL: never stores from an unconfirmed trial (confirmed_outcome must be True)
        end
    end
